# Match Flow and Scoring

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M2 Vertical slice
Dependencies: `02_DOMAIN_RULES.todo`, `04_TERRITORY_PAINTING.todo`, pressure decision in `15_PRODUCT_DECISIONS.todo`

## Purpose

Deliver a complete match from start through result and rematch with explainable scoring.

## Tasks

- [x] Implement match bootstrap.
- [x] Implement countdown and active phase.
- [x] Implement timer.
- [x] Implement selected pressure mechanism.
- [x] Implement active-arena coverage calculation.
- [x] Implement bank display data.
- [x] Implement explicit tie behavior.
- [x] Implement result snapshot.
- [x] Implement reset and rematch.
- [x] Emit phase and result events.
- [x] Add ten-match automated smoke scenario.
- [x] Test zero ownership, ties, reset, and completion.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Ten consecutive matches complete without manual repair.
- [x] Result matches authoritative territory state.
- [x] Tie and zero-owner behavior is explicit.
- [ ] Pressure is telegraphed and symmetric.
- [x] Rematch returns to a clean state.
- [ ] Result data explains decisive territory and reactions.

## Completion evidence

Implementation is complete; developer hands-on approval of pressure readability, result comprehension,
and the complete interactive loop remains required. Automated symmetry, pressure text, and result data
checks pass, but do not replace that review.

- 2026-09-10: full initial bot/match baseline passed 180 EditMode and 44 PlayMode tests.
  Subsequent bot-opponent preference checks passed 69 policy cases and 9 competitive-bot PlayMode tests,
  including ten live rounds; see TODO 07 and docs/16_COMPETITIVE_BOTS.md.
- Ten consecutive simulated 120-second matches cover winners, bank-independent ties, and zero ownership.
- Windows development build succeeded; the built arena initialized with Direct3D 11 and stayed running
  without runtime/shader errors. The owned smoke-test player was stopped.
- Active coverage averaged 0.319 ms per refresh across 100 warm samples in the full baseline run.
- HUD text bounds, major-panel non-overlap, and virtual keyboard/gamepad controls passed.
- Documentation and review checklist: `docs/15_MATCH_FLOW_SCORING.md`.
- Match config: `EntropyTag/Assets/EntropyTag/Settings/Tuning/FirstSliceMatch.asset`.
- Latest evidence: ignored `EntropyTag/TestResults/` XML/logs and `EntropyTag/Builds/Windows-development.log`.
- No minimum-spec GPU/FPS or human readability claim is made.
- Canonical context synchronization is pending because this base is absent from the current Context Mesh
  registry. Its `.agent-context` remains read-only; the implementation handoff is saved in session artifacts.
- Changes are uncommitted on `workDesk/agentic`. The developer subsequently authorized two mobile bots;
  TODO 07 now provides a real three-player contested match for the remaining review.

## Completion log

- 2026-09-10 - Started after the developer authorized the next implementation with Unity closed. Preserve
  free play until an explicit match start, lock team choice during the match, score upward-facing logical
  cells inside a circular shrinking boundary, use non-lethal out-of-bounds recovery, and keep the bot parked.
- 2026-09-10 - Implemented and validated the solo match proof, regenerated the selected sandbox and buildable
  arena, updated documentation/ledger, and stopped at the hands-on approval gate. Status remains IN_PROGRESS.
- 2026-09-10 - Integrated the developer-authorized Ice/Fire competitive bots without changing match victory
  rules. Ten live-physics bot matches now complement the original injected-state scoring scenarios.
